-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 17.5.2009 (הסתדרות המורים) — מענק יוח"א לשנות הלימודים
-- התשס"ח והתשס"ט: the agreement of 30.8.2006 on the long-school-day grant
-- (יום חינוך ארוך, "יוח"א"), carried into 5768 and 5769 and fitted to the
-- Ofek Hadash reform (preamble). It runs from 1.9.2007 to 31.8.2009 (§2) and
-- reaches the State's teaching-scale employees in the primary schools and
-- kindergartens that run the long day and are assigned to its hours (§3).
-- §4: which hours are the long day's, who is owed the grant — a teacher
-- outside the reform assigned with his consent, a teacher in it required to
-- teach in the seventh and eighth hours — the full grant for eight weekly
-- hours and its share for fewer, none for a period of reserve duty or
-- maternity leave, 6,300 or 4,700 a year whatever the position, paid in May
-- and June, and contributions to a provident fund; exhaustion, the
-- disputes, industrial peace and the earlier terms (§§5–8); and the wages
-- commissioner's letter that the grant is not counted in the erosion checks.
--
-- Why it is here: §4.3 takes the grant's share for the time on maternity
-- leave or reserve duty, and only for those, which the Equal Opportunities
-- Law forbids (MMS-601; a card on the contradictions page).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT equal_opportunities_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — מענק יוח"א לשנות הלימודים התשס"ח והתשס"ט (הסתדרות המורים, 17.5.2009)`

DECLARE `long-day grant action` IS ONE OF
    `assign a teacher outside the reform to the long day's hours`
    `strike over the long-day grant`
    `lock out over the long-day grant`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The registration stamp, partly illegible, dated 15.9.2003 on its face, its number handwritten; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 The State and who represents it (the wages commissioner and the director-general of the Ministry of Education); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 The State's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p6 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p7 הסתדרות המורים and its secretary-general; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p8 The union's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 "It was therefore agreed"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 A fax banner; no rule.

-- ¶3: made and signed on 17.5.2009, the day written in by hand.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the long-day grant agreement of 5768–5769 was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 5 2009

-- ¶10–12: the agreement of 30.8.2006 paid the grant to teachers assigned to
-- the long school day under the Long School Day and Enrichment Studies Law,
-- 1997, in 5767 (outside the corpus); the reform is applied from 5768 under
-- the agreements of 10.9.2007 and 25.12.2008; the parties carry the 2006
-- understandings into 5768 and 5769, fitted to the reform where it applies.
@ref akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12
`what the long-day grant agreement of 5768–5769 rests on outside the corpus` MEANS
    LIST `outside the corpus` "הסכם יוח\"א תשס\"ז (ההסכם מיום 30.8.2006 בדבר תשלום מענק יוח\"א)",
         `outside the corpus` "חוק יום חינוך ארוך ולימודי העשרה, התשנ\"ז-1997"

-- §1: the preamble is part of the agreement.
@ref akn:art_1 akn:art_1/p1
`the long-day grant agreement's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2 תקופת ההסכם`

-- From 1.9.2007 to 31.8.2009, both days in it (convention dates.end).
@ref akn:art_2 akn:art_2/p1
`the long-day grant agreement runs from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2007
`the long-day grant agreement runs until` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2009

§§ `3 תחולת ההסכם`

-- Every State employee in the teaching scale employed in a primary school
-- or a kindergarten that runs the long day and assigned to it in 5768 or
-- 5769 ("עובדי ההוראה").
@ref akn:art_3 akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN `in the teaching scale, in the State's service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a primary school or kindergarten that runs the long day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assigned to the long day in 5768 or 5769` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the long-day grant agreement applies to` `in the teaching scale, in the State's service` `in a primary school or kindergarten that runs the long day` `assigned to the long day in 5768 or 5769` IF
        `in the teaching scale, in the State's service`
    AND `in a primary school or kindergarten that runs the long day`
    AND `assigned to the long day in 5768 or 5769`

§§ `4 מענק יוח"א`

-- 4.1: the long day's hours — in a primary school, the seventh and eighth
-- hours of the day; in a kindergarten, 13:20 to 15:30 until 31.12.07 and
-- 13:30 to 15:30 from 1.1.08 to 31.8.2009 (minutes from midnight).
@ref akn:art_4 akn:art_4__para_4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-1/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-1/p3
`the long day's hours in a primary school` MEANS LIST 7, 8

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-1/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-1/p6
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the long day starts in a kindergarten, in minutes from midnight` `the day` IS
    IF `the day` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2007)
    THEN 13 TIMES 60 PLUS 20
    ELSE 13 TIMES 60 PLUS 30

`the long day ends in a kindergarten, in minutes from midnight` MEANS 15 TIMES 60 PLUS 30

-- 4.2(א): a teacher outside the reform, assigned with his consent in 5768
-- and/or 5769 to frontal teaching in the long day's hours, whose position
-- outside them is no smaller than his hours in them, is paid a one-time
-- grant for the year he is assigned — the whole of it for eight weekly
-- hours, its share for fewer. 4.2(ב): a teacher under the reform's terms,
-- in a school that runs the long day, required by his weekly timetable to
-- teach frontal hours (as the reform agreements define them) in the
-- seventh and eighth hours — the whole of it for eight, its share for fewer.
-- (ב)'s entitlement prints "התשס"ה" where its opening reads "התשס"ח"; the
-- rule asks only whether he is required in a year the agreement runs (§2),
-- so nothing turns on which the clause meant.
@desc A teacher's long day in a school year, as §4.2 asks about it.
DECLARE `a teacher's long day` HAS
    `under the reform's terms`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `assigned with his consent`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc outside the reform (4.2(א), 4.10)
    `required by his timetable to teach in the seventh and eighth hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc under the reform (4.2(ב))
    `weekly frontal hours in the long day`           IS A NUMBER
    `weekly hours outside the long day`              IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_a akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_a/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_b akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_b/p2
GIVEN t IS A `a teacher's long day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owed the long-day grant` t IF
        t's `weekly frontal hours in the long day` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (IF t's `under the reform's terms`
         THEN t's `required by his timetable to teach in the seventh and eighth hours`
         ELSE     t's `assigned with his consent`
              AND t's `weekly hours outside the long day` AT LEAST t's `weekly frontal hours in the long day`)

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_a/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_b/p2
GIVEN t IS A `a teacher's long day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the long-day grant for his hours` t IS
    IF `owed the long-day grant` t
    THEN min 1 (t's `weekly frontal hours in the long day` DIVIDED BY 8)
    ELSE 0

-- 4.3: notwithstanding the section, a teacher is not owed the grant's share
-- for a period of reserve duty or of maternity leave; one whose employment
-- ended in the year is owed the share for the time he was employed. Any
-- other absence — an illness, unpaid leave, a strike — the section does not
-- name, and it takes nothing from the grant.
DECLARE `absence in the long-day year` IS ONE OF
    `reserve duty in the long-day year`
    `maternity leave in the long-day year`
    `illness in the long-day year`
    `another absence in the long-day year`

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3
GIVEN a IS AN `absence in the long-day year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4.3 takes the grant's share for` a IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `reserve duty in the long-day year` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `maternity leave in the long-day year` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- akn:art_4__para_4-3/p2 A fax banner; no rule.

-- 4.4: the grant for each of 5768 and 5769 — 6,300 outside the reform,
-- 4,700 under it. 4.5: whatever the position. 4.3 and 4.2 together: the
-- year's grant times the share for his hours, times the share of the year
-- he was employed, less the share he spent on reserve duty or maternity
-- leave.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4 akn:art_4__para_4-4/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-4/p3
GIVEN `under the reform's terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the long-day grant for a year` `under the reform's terms` IS
    IF `under the reform's terms` THEN 4700 ELSE 6300

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-5
`the long-day grant does not depend on the position` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-5
GIVEN t IS A `a teacher's long day`
      `share of the year employed` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 where he was employed all year; his share where his employment ended in it
      `share of the year absent` IS A NUMBER @desc the part of the year he was absent
      a IS AN `absence in the long-day year` @desc what the absence was
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the long-day grant he is owed` t `share of the year employed` `share of the year absent` a IS
    `the long-day grant for a year` (t's `under the reform's terms`)
        TIMES `the share of the long-day grant for his hours` t
        TIMES (`share of the year employed` MINUS `the share 4.3 takes`)
    WHERE
        `the share 4.3 takes` MEANS
            IF `section 4.3 takes the grant's share for` a THEN `share of the year absent` ELSE 0

-- 4.6: 9/10 of the grant is paid with the salary of May (2008 or 2009),
-- spread over his months of work from September to May; 1/10 with June's.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6
`the share of the long-day grant paid with May's salary` MEANS 9 DIVIDED BY 10
`the share of the long-day grant paid with June's salary` MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY 10

-- 4.7: what was paid for 5768 counts as paid under this agreement and on
-- account of what it owes.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-7
GIVEN `owed for 5768` IS A NUMBER, `already paid for 5768` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the long-day grant left to pay for 5768` `owed for 5768` `already paid for 5768` IS
    max 0 (`owed for 5768` MINUS `already paid for 5768`)

-- 4.8: on the grant, contributions and deductions to a provident fund that
-- does not pay an annuity — 5% the employer's, 5% the employee's — by the
-- principles of the agreement of 17.12.1998.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-8
`the employer's provident-fund rate on the long-day grant` MEANS 5%
`the employee's provident-fund rate on the long-day grant` MEANS 5%

-- 4.9: that a teacher is employed in a school or kindergarten that runs the
-- long day does not of itself entitle him to the grant (4.2 decides).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-9
`employment where the long day runs entitles to the long-day grant of itself` MEANS FALSE

-- 4.10: a teacher outside the reform is assigned to the long day's hours
-- only with his consent.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-10
GIVEN `under the reform's terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `long-day grant action`
DECIDE `assigning to the long day's hours` `under the reform's terms` `consented` IS
    IF `under the reform's terms` OR `consented`
    THEN PARTY `the State`
         MAY   `assign a teacher outside the reform to the long day's hours`
    ELSE PARTY `the State`
         SHANT `assign a teacher outside the reform to the long day's hours`

-- 4.11: if the Minister of Education sets another number of hours for the
-- long day in primary schools than §3(ב) of the law sets, moving a seventh
-- or eighth hour to another day, the moved hour is a long-day hour for a
-- teacher outside the reform.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-11
GIVEN `moved by the Minister from the seventh or eighth hour of another day` IS A BOOLEAN, `under the reform's terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a moved hour is a long-day hour` `moved by the Minister from the seventh or eighth hour of another day` `under the reform's terms` IF
    `moved by the Minister from the seventh or eighth hour of another day` AND (NOT `under the reform's terms`)

-- not weighed against `the Women's Work Law`: §4.3 does not give the
-- grant's share for maternity leave (nor for reserve duty); the grant is
-- paid for the seventh and eighth hours the teacher is assigned to, and in
-- the birth and parenthood period she is not employed (§8 of the law) and
-- her employer pays her nothing — maternity pay is the National Insurance
-- Institute's; §6(ט) keeps the rights that depend on seniority, and a grant
-- for the hours taught is not one: no floor of that law is gone below.
-- Against the Equal Opportunities Law it is weighed below (F-yocha-2009-a).

-- F-yocha-2009-a: the Equal Opportunities Law (imported), §2. §4.3 takes
-- the grant's share for the time a teacher was on maternity leave or on
-- reserve duty, and for no other absence: a teacher away ill for the same
-- months keeps the whole grant. §2(א) names among its grounds pregnancy,
-- being a parent and reserve service, in pay and the conditions of work
-- ((א)(2)); the job does not require the line (§2(ג)), and §3(א), which
-- keeps a provision "in connection with" birth, is read as keeping one that
-- protects the employee, not one that takes pay from her for it (convention
-- instruments.pregnancy-provision, a pick for the lawyer). The law governs
-- (`the ruling under the statutes' floor`; convention
-- instruments.statute-floor): she is owed the grant as one absent ill is.
-- Placeholders: eight hours outside the reform, a whole year employed,
-- three tenths of it away.
`the full long day outside the reform` MEANS
    `a teacher's long day` WITH
        `under the reform's terms`                       IS FALSE
        `assigned with his consent`                      IS TRUE
        `required by his timetable to teach in the seventh and eighth hours` IS FALSE
        `weekly frontal hours in the long day`           IS 8
        `weekly hours outside the long day`              IS 16

`section 4.3 takes from maternity leave and reserve duty what it leaves an illness, which section 2 forbids` MEANS
        `the long-day grant he is owed` `the full long day outside the reform` 1 0.3 `maternity leave in the long-day year`
        LESS THAN `the long-day grant he is owed` `the full long day outside the reform` 1 0.3 `illness in the long-day year`
    AND `the long-day grant he is owed` `the full long day outside the reform` 1 0.3 `reserve duty in the long-day year`
        LESS THAN `the long-day grant he is owed` `the full long day outside the reform` 1 0.3 `illness in the long-day year`
    AND `discrimination under section 2` TRUE FALSE (`section 3 keeps it from being discrimination` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 4.3 takes from maternity leave and reserve duty what it leaves an illness, which section 2 forbids`

§§ `5–8 מיצוי, סכסוכים, שקט תעשייתי ותנאים קודמים`

-- §5: a full and final exhaustion of the parties' claims on what it
-- settles, for its period. §6: the collective disputes declared or notified
-- by its signing, on what it settles, are void. §7: neither side strikes or
-- locks out over it for its period. §8: the terms the parties set before
-- stand, unless it changed or cancelled them.
@ref akn:art_5 akn:art_5/p1
`the long-day grant agreement exhausts the claims it settles` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_6 akn:art_6/p1
`the disputes over the long-day grant are void on its signing` MEANS TRUE

-- akn:art_7/p1 A fax banner; no rule.

@ref akn:art_7 akn:art_7/p2
`industrial peace over the long-day grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `strike over the long-day grant`

`the State's industrial peace over the long-day grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    SHANT `lock out over the long-day grant`

@ref akn:art_8 akn:art_8/p1
`the earlier terms stand beside the long-day grant agreement` MEANS TRUE

